What is the Trading Cards Market?
Trading cards are collectible items typically made of paperboard or thick paper, featuring images of people, places, or fictional characters along with descriptive text and game statistics. These cards serve three primary purposes: competitive gameplay (TCGs/CCGs), entertainment collectibles, and investment assets. The market spans multiple categories including sports cards, entertainment IP cards, and competitive battle card games, with rare editions often commanding premium valuations in secondary markets.
