Regional Market Insights
•	North America: Maintains leadership with 45% global share, driven by robust sports card culture and mature grading/auction infrastructure. The U.S. dominates high-end transactions while Canada shows strong hockey card demand.
•	Europe: Shows divided preferences with the UK favoring football (soccer) cards, Germany preferring TCGs, and Eastern Europe emerging as a production hub for competitive game cards.
•	Asia-Pacific: The fastest-growing region led by Japan's Pokémon/Yu-Gi-Oh! ecosystems and China's booming domestic IP collectibles. South Korea demonstrates unique hybrid demand across K-pop and esports categories.
•	Latin America: Concentrated around football cards with Brazil and Argentina as key markets, though economic volatility impacts premium segment growth.
•	Middle East & Africa: Nascent but promising, with UAE collectors driving luxury card imports and South Africa maintaining niche cricket/rugby collector communities.
